        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-15T23:08:26Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(xtask): share one job budget across the lanes of a gate wave\n\nThe release tier ran up to four lanes, each with -j 6 and\n--test-threads=6: up to 24 compile jobs on a 6-job machine.\n\n- budget.rs: one budget (default 6, CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS overrides).\n- A wave of N lanes gives each lane budget/N jobs (minimum 1); a wave\n  holds at most budget/2 lanes; a step alone keeps the full budget.\n- The executor rewrites -j and --test-threads per step at run time, so\n  the plan builders (and open PR #1952) stay unchanged.\n- The gate prints the budget and the jobs of each wave, also in\n  --dry-run.\n- gate and runners skills: the sum of -j of all builds on one machine\n  stays at or below its core count.\n\nFixes #2057\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
